{"product_id":"steve-jobs-the-man-who-thought-different","title":"Steve Jobs: The Man Who Thought Different","description":"\u003cp data-start=\"191\" data-end=\"494\"\u003eSome people see the world as it is. Steve Jobs saw it as it \u003cem data-start=\"251\" data-end=\"261\"\u003ecould be\u003c\/em\u003e—sleeker, sharper, smarter, and infinitely cooler. Long before Apple became the planet’s pocket-sized religion, Jobs was just a college dropout with a knack for imagination and an uncanny ability to turn “what if?” into “why not?”.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp data-start=\"496\" data-end=\"934\"\u003eIn \u003cem data-start=\"499\" data-end=\"542\"\u003eSteve Jobs: The Man Who Thought Different\u003c\/em\u003e, award-winning journalist Karen Blumenthal tells the extraordinary story of the boy who grew up tinkering in garages and ended up reshaping entire industries—computers, music, phones, even the way we think about fonts. This isn’t a sanitized fairy tale; it’s the real journey of a visionary who was rebellious, brilliant, sometimes difficult, but always daring enough to think differently.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp data-start=\"936\" data-end=\"1266\"\u003ePacked with inspiration (and the occasional reality check), this book isn’t just about technology—it’s about courage, creativity, and what it takes to change the world. Whether you’re a teen just starting to dream or an adult who secretly still wants to change everything, Jobs’ story is a masterclass in chasing the impossible.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp data-start=\"1268\" data-end=\"1402\"\u003eProduct details\u003cbr data-start=\"1283\" data-end=\"1286\"\u003eAuthor: Karen Blumenthal\u003cbr data-start=\"1310\" data-end=\"1313\"\u003eFormat: Paperback\u003cbr data-start=\"1330\" data-end=\"1333\"\u003ePages: 320\u003cbr data-start=\"1343\" data-end=\"1346\"\u003eISBN: 9781408832066\u003cbr data-start=\"1365\" data-end=\"1368\"\u003eDimensions: 19.8 x 12.9 x 2.1 cm\u003c\/p\u003e","brand":"bookloopbook.com","offers":[{"